{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Machinery.QPochhammer","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Machinery.QPochhammer","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Group.Finset.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.GeomSum"],"declarations":10,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.qBinomial_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.qBinomial_zero","kind":"theorem","line":124,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/QPochhammer.lean#L124-L132","doc":"`[n 0]_q = 1`, provided the diagonal q-Pochhammer `(q;q)_n` is\nnonzero (needed so the quotient `(q;q)_n / (q;q)_n` cancels to `1`;\n`qBinomial` is defined as a real quotient and is not totalized at the\n`(q;q)_n = 0` locus, e.g. roots of unity). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.qBinomial","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.qBinomial","kind":"def","line":117,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/QPochhammer.lean#L117-L122","doc":"**Gaussian q-binomial** `[n k]_q` as a quotient of q-Pochhammers (standard\n`(q;q)` normalization — see the normalization note above; distinct from the\nbalanced canonical `QPartitionCombinatorics.qBinom`).\nWell-defined when `(q;q)_k ≠ 0` and `(q;q)_{n-k} ≠ 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.qPochhammerDiag_at_q_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.qPochhammerDiag_at_q_one","kind":"theorem","line":95,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/QPochhammer.lean#L95-L102","doc":"**At q = 1**, `(q;q)_n = 0` for all `n ≥ 1` because the `k = 0`\nfactor is `1 - q^1 = 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.qPochhammerFinite_succ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.qPochhammerFinite_succ","kind":"theorem","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/QPochhammer.lean#L87-L93","doc":"**Recursion**: `(a;q)_{n+1} = (a;q)_n · (1 - a·q^n)`. Direct\napplication of `Finset.prod_range_succ` (the term closes the goal up\nto beta-reduction of `f n`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.qPochhammerDiag_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.qPochhammerDiag_one","kind":"theorem","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/QPochhammer.lean#L82-L85","doc":"**(q;q)_1 = 1 - q**. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.qPochhammerDiag_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.qPochhammerDiag_zero","kind":"theorem","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/QPochhammer.lean#L77-L80","doc":"**(q;q)_0 = 1** (empty product). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.qPochhammerFinite_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.qPochhammerFinite_one","kind":"theorem","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/QPochhammer.lean#L71-L75","doc":"**(a;q)_1 = 1 - a**. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.qPochhammerFinite_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.qPochhammerFinite_zero","kind":"theorem","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/QPochhammer.lean#L65-L69","doc":"**(a;q)_0 = 1** (empty product). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.qPochhammerDiag","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.qPochhammerDiag","kind":"def","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/QPochhammer.lean#L55-L61","doc":"Diagonal q-Pochhammer `(q;q)_n`, defined as `qPochhammerFinite q q n\n= ∏_{k=0}^{n-1} (1 - q·q^k)`. Note this equals the textbook form\n`∏_{k=0}^{n-1} (1 - q^(k+1))` (provably, via `q·q^k = q^(k+1)`), but the\ntwo are not definitionally equal — we keep the `q·q^k` form so that\n`qPochhammerDiag` reuses `qPochhammerFinite` directly. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.qPochhammerFinite","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.qPochhammerFinite","kind":"def","line":51,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/QPochhammer.lean#L51-L53","doc":"Finite q-Pochhammer `(a;q)_n = ∏_{k=0}^{n-1} (1 - a·q^k)`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}